PART 3: DUAL-USE AND PROTECTIVE SAFEGUARDS
================================================================================
The mathematical primitives of this architecture manage connection fields, trajectory tracking, and error-filtering metrics inside multi-dimensional manifolds. Because these coordinates are inherently dual-use and structurally identical to target localization and autonomous routing vectors, the following execution conditions are permanently attached to this software:

1. Non-Offensive Optimization: The manifold metrics, vector fields, and tracking scripts contained herein may not be used for offensive kinetic targeting, launch-vector planning, hyper-adversarial strike configurations, or automated weapon swarm coordination.
2. Passive Defense & Civilian Preservation: Deployment within live hardware systems is strictly limited to non-military, passive defensive protection, such as shielding public infrastructure, civilian transport networks, energy grids, and human-centered utility frameworks from structural defects, data corruption, or external hazards.
3. Provenance Integrity: Any downstream software adaptation that adapts these geometric primitives for automated coordination tools must preserve this safeguard block, preventing the co-optation of the parent math by military-industrial or offensive state actors.

================================================================================
PART 4: COGNITIVE AND TECHNICAL BOUNDARY DISCLAIMER
================================================================================
All structural reference parameters, 80D soft Riemannian tensors, and algebraic primitives contained within this dual configuration are formalized strictly as visual layout coordinates, creative proof-state boundaries, and mathematical safeguards against semantic mimicry and floating-point drift cascades on an isolated goal stack. These metrics are not certified or safety-tested for aerospace guidance, real-world tactical control, or high-stakes physical autonomy. Downstream implementations are entirely "as-is" and remain subject to the smart-contract, utility-token, and regulatory disclosures maintained at vaked.dev/legal.
